const report=`# Global production rank-gradient audit\n\nFreeze date: ${FREEZE_DATE}  \nCode baseline: \`main@${HEAD}\`  \nProtocol fingerprint: \`${protocolHash}\`  \nHistory fingerprint: \`${historyHash}\`\n\n## Research question\n\nDoes the complete Production rank 1-10 contain stable ordinal information about subsequent digit appearance? This is not a Win-set strategy test.\n\n## Difference from prior frozen work\n\nThe miss-structure audit compared only ranks 7-10 after exclusion from Win 6. This audit measures the full rank 1-10 gradient. Rank Consensus, score-gap, Hot/Cold, and family audits remain frozen and are not reinterpreted.\n\n## Production contract and pool\n\n- Source: \`src/lib/analysis/global-daily-sources.ts#GLOBAL_DAILY_SOURCE_IDS\`; **${POOL.length} lotteries at main@${HEAD}**.\n- Exact IDs: ${POOL.map((id)=>`\`${id}\``).join(", ")}\n- Exact \`buildGlobalWeekdayWin\`: same weekday, maximum ${GLOBAL_WEEKDAY_LOOKBACK} prior observations per lottery, presence per draw/side, per-lottery normalization, equal available-side weighting, deterministic score/top+bottom/digit ordering.\n\n## Frozen analysis\n\n- Primary statistic: unweighted mean target-date Spearman correlation between ranks 1-10 and future either-side appearance rates; negative indicates expected ordinal direction.\n- Uniform references: 19.00% per side and 34.39% either-side for independent uniform digits.\n- Digit adjustment: prior-only expanding marginal for each digit; residual observed either presence minus prior marginal.\n- Adjacent tie tolerance: exactly zero. Chronological 75/25 split; ${BOOTSTRAPS.toLocaleString("en-US")} target-date cluster bootstrap iterations.\n- No alternative strategy, weight, window, pool, threshold, or model was tested.\n\n## Data\n\n- Range: ${result.data.range[0]} to ${result.data.range[1]}\n- Dates: ${result.data.targetDates}; outcomes: ${result.data.outcomes}; sides: ${result.data.sides}\n- Stored sources: ${result.data.storedSources}/${POOL.length}; read-only hydration: ${result.data.readOnlyHydratedSources.join(", ")||"none"}\n\n## Full rank table - all\n\n| Rank | Opportunities | Top | Top rate | Bottom | Bottom rate | Either | Either rate | Marginal-adjusted |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${rankTable("all")}\n\nDevelopment and Holdout full tables follow.\n\n### Development\n${rankTable("development")}\n\n### Holdout\n${rankTable("holdout")}\n\n## Primary ordinal statistic and uncertainty\n\n- All mean date-level Spearman: **${all.primarySpearman.toFixed(3)}**, 95% CI **${ci(confidence.all.spearman)}**.\n- Development: ${sections.development.primarySpearman.toFixed(3)}; Holdout: ${sections.holdout.primarySpearman.toFixed(3)}.\n- Pooled-rank Spearman (descriptive): ${all.pooledSpearman.toFixed(3)}.\n\n## Adjacent monotonicity\n\nDecreases ${all.adjacent.decreases}/9; exact ties ${all.adjacent.ties}/9; reversals ${all.adjacent.reversals}/9. Largest expected step after rank ${all.adjacent.largestExpected.afterRank}: ${signed(all.adjacent.largestExpected.difference)}; largest reversal after rank ${all.adjacent.largestReversal.afterRank}: ${signed(all.adjacent.largestReversal.difference)}.\n\n## Five equal rank bands\n\n| Band | Top | Bottom | Either | Marginal-adjusted either |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${bandTable("all")}\n\n## High / Middle / Low and split\n\n| Section | Dates | Outcomes | Mean Spearman | High 1-2 | Middle 5-6 | Low 9-10 | High-Low | Adjusted High-Low |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${sectionTable}\n\nAll-data 95% CIs: High ${pct(confidence.all.high[0])} to ${pct(confidence.all.high[1])}; Middle ${pct(confidence.all.middle[0])} to ${pct(confidence.all.middle[1])}; Low ${pct(confidence.all.low[0])} to ${pct(confidence.all.low[1])}; High-Low ${signed(confidence.all.highMinusLow[0])} to ${signed(confidence.all.highMinusLow[1])}; adjusted High-Low ${signed(confidence.all.adjustedHighMinusLow[0])} to ${signed(confidence.all.adjustedHighMinusLow[1])}.\n\n## Digit identity confound\n\n| Digit | Mean rank | Median rank | Rank 1-2 share | Rank 1-6 share | Target either rate | Within-digit Spearman |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${digitTable}\n\nThe prior-only adjusted gradient distinguishes daily ordering from persistent digit identity without fitting a prediction model.\n\n## Monthly stability\n\n| Month | Dates | Outcomes | Spearman | High | Middle | Low | High-Low |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${monthTable}\n\n## Weekday stability\n\n| Weekday | Dates | Outcomes | Spearman | High | Middle | Low | High-Low |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n${weekdayTable}\n\n## Top versus bottom\n\nThe full table reports top and bottom separately for every rank and every band. Existing 50:50 Production weighting is unchanged.\n\n## Lottery heterogeneity\n\nMinimum ${lotterySummary.minimumOutcomes} outcomes: ${lotterySummary.eligible}/${POOL.length} eligible; positive High-Low ${lotterySummary.positive}, zero ${lotterySummary.zero}, negative ${lotterySummary.negative}; median ${signed(lotterySummary.median)}. Extremes are inspection-only.\n\n| Lottery | Outcomes | High-Low |\n|---|---:|---:|\n${lotteryTable}\n\n## Frozen interpretation\n\n**${interpretation}**\n\nUX implication for descriptive High/Middle/Low labels: **${uxImplication}**. A higher Production score may be described as a higher historical rank; it must not be translated into a greater probability of appearing unless the evidence supports that separate claim. No UI change is authorized.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Rankings are relative among only ten digits; identities have unequal marginals and scores are often flat.\n- Adjacent ranks can have tiny score differences; repeated ranks and outcomes on the same date are correlated.\n- Lotteries and shared market sessions may not be independent.\n- Storage completeness limits the period; all ${POOL.length} sources were available here.\n- Monthly, weekday, side, digit, and lottery slices are descriptive and can show chance patterns.\n- Ordinal association is not probability or proof of prediction; retrospective evidence need not persist.\n\n## Contract confirmation\n\n- Production formula changed: **NO**\n- Production pool changed: **NO**\n- Production UI changed: **NO**\n- Prospective tracking added: **NO**\n- New strategy tested: **NO**\n`;
